{"name":"White Fence","hex":"#f2e9d3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"},{"term":"fence","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thin artificial barrier that separates two pieces of land or forms a perimeter enclosing the lands of a house, building, etc.","Someone who hides or buys and sells stolen goods, a criminal middleman for transactions of stolen goods."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enclose, contain or separate by building fence.","To defend or guard."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fence"}],"entries":[{"title":"White Fence","blocks":[{"text":"White Fence is a predominantly Mexican American street gang in the Boyle Heights neighborhood of East Los Angeles."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Fence","wikidata":"Q7994682"},{"title":"Fence","blocks":[{"text":"A fence is a structure that encloses an area, typically outdoors creating a boundary, and is usually constructed from posts that are connected by boards, wire, rails or netting. A fence differs from a wall in not having a solid foundation along its whole length."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Westtown.jpg/330px-Westtown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fence","wikidata":"Q148571"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Railroad_tracks_through_East_Germany_in_1977.jpg/500px-Railroad_tracks_through_East_Germany_in_1977.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Railroad_tracks_through_East_Germany_in_1977.jpg/1280px-Railroad_tracks_through_East_Germany_in_1977.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Railroad_tracks_through_East_Germany_in_1977.jpg/500px-Railroad_tracks_through_East_Germany_in_1977.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"During the Cold War, West German trains ran through East Germany. This 1977 view shows how East German authorities placed fences near the tracks to keep potential defectors at bay","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARailroad_tracks_through_East_Germany_in_1977.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Barbed_Wire%2C_SC%2C_Victoria%2C_15.9.2007.jpg/500px-Barbed_Wire%2C_SC%2C_Victoria%2C_15.9.2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Barbed_Wire%2C_SC%2C_Victoria%2C_15.9.2007.jpg/1280px-Barbed_Wire%2C_SC%2C_Victoria%2C_15.9.2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&